---
import SimLayout from '../../../layouts/SimLayout.astro';
---

<SimLayout
  areaSlug="electronics"
  title="Memristor"
  description="A resistor that remembers how much charge went through it. Inside is a thin film with a boundary you can watch move: push current one way and the conducting layer grows, push it back and it shrinks, stop pushing and it stays exactly where you left it. Drive it with a sine wave and the current-voltage curve is not a line but a loop pinched at the origin, the fingerprint no resistor, capacitor or inductor can produce."
>
  <div class="sim">
    <div class="sim-stage">
      <canvas id="mr" class="mr-canvas" width="1000" height="880"></canvas>
    </div>

    <div class="sim-panel">
      <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap">
        <button class="btn" id="run">Pause</button>
        <button class="btn ghost" id="reset">Reset</button>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Source</label>
        <div class="seg" id="src">
          <button data-s="manual" class="active">Manual</button>
          <button data-s="ac">AC</button>
          <button data-s="pulse">Pulses</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label><span id="vlab">Drive it yourself</span> <b id="vsval">0.00 V</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="vs" min="-150" max="150" step="1" value="0" />
        <div class="scale-hint"><span id="vhint">drag me up and down</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="control" id="ctl-f">
        <label>Frequency <b id="fval">—</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="freq" min="10" max="600" step="5" value="100" />
        <div class="scale-hint"><span>slow, fat loop</span><span>fast, thin loop</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>R_on (fully doped) <b id="ronval">—</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="ron" min="20" max="400" step="10" value="100" />
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>R_off (fully undoped) <b id="roffval">—</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="roff" min="10" max="400" step="5" value="160" />
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Film thickness D <b id="dval">10 nm</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="d" min="5" max="30" step="1" value="10" />
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Ion mobility µ_v <b id="muval">—</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="mu" min="20" max="300" step="5" value="100" />
        <div class="scale-hint"><span>sluggish</span><span>eager</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Boundary</label>
        <div class="seg" id="win">
          <button data-w="hard" class="active">Hard stop</button>
          <button data-w="soft">Sticky</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Time rate <b id="rateval">1.0×</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="rate" min="10" max="300" step="5" value="100" />
      </div>

      <div class="readout">
        <div class="row"><span id="l1">—</span><b id="r1">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l2">—</span><b id="r2">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l3">—</span><b id="r3">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l4">—</span><b id="r4">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l5">—</span><b id="r5">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l6">—</span><b id="r6">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l7">—</span><b id="r7">—</b></div>
      </div>

      <p style="font-size:.82rem;color:var(--text-faint);margin:0;line-height:1.5">
        Each dot is an oxygen vacancy you can count, and the boundary between the
        doped and undoped halves is the device's entire memory. Everything else on
        screen is measured from it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Fragment slot="observe">
    <li>
      Start in Manual and push the slider up. Vacancies drift to the right, the
      doped layer eats into the undoped one, and the resistance falls as it goes.
      Now <b>let the slider go back to zero</b>. The current stops, the drift
      stops, and the boundary <b>stays exactly where you left it</b>. That is the
      whole idea: a resistor whose value is the running total of the charge you
      have pushed through it.
    </li>
    <li>
      Push the slider down instead and the boundary walks back. The state has no
      preferred direction and no restoring force, unlike a capacitor, which
      always wants to discharge. Nothing here is stored as energy, only as
      <b>position</b>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Switch to <b>AC</b> and watch the current-voltage panel. It is not a
      straight line and it is not an ellipse: it is a loop that crosses itself
      and is <b>pinched shut at the origin</b>. It has to be. The voltage is
      M·i and M is finite, so when the current is zero the voltage is zero too.
      No resistor, capacitor or inductor can draw that shape.
    </li>
    <li>
      Now raise the frequency and watch the loop <b>collapse towards a straight
      line</b>. Faster driving gives the boundary less time to move within a
      cycle, so the resistance barely changes and the device degenerates into an
      ordinary resistor. A memristor only looks like a memristor when you drive
      it slowly enough for its memory to matter.
    </li>
    <li>
      The right-hand panel is the definition rather than a consequence. Charge is
      the running total of current and flux linkage the running total of voltage,
      and the traced points sit on <b>one fixed curve</b> in that plane whatever
      you do to the drive: sine, pulses or by hand. Its slope is M. Resistance,
      capacitance and inductance are the slopes of the other three such curves.
    </li>
    <li>
      Turn the amplitude up until the boundary slams into either end. The
      resistance flattens out at R_on or R_off, the loop develops straight
      segments, and the device stops remembering because there is nowhere left to
      move. That saturation is what makes it a usable memory cell rather than a
      curiosity: switch <b>Pulses</b> on and watch it latch between two states.
    </li>
    <li>
      Set the boundary to <b>Sticky</b>. A real dopant boundary slows as it nears
      an edge, so the drift is throttled there. Drive it hard into a rail and it
      can no longer come back at all: the state gets <b>stuck</b> against the
      wall, which is the well-known failure of the simplest window models and the
      reason the choice of window function is not a cosmetic detail.
    </li>
  </Fragment>
</SimLayout>

<script>
  import { setupCanvas, makeText, subHtml } from '../../../lib/sim';

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // The HP / Strukov thin-film model. A film of thickness D is split into a
  // doped region of width w (oxygen vacancies present, conducting) and an
  // undoped one (insulating). The vacancies are charged, so current drags the
  // boundary along with it, and the resistance is whatever the two layers make
  // in series.
  //
  //      x = w/D            M(x) = R_on x + R_off (1 - x)
  //      dw/dt = µ_v (R_on/D) i      so      dx/dt = (µ_v R_on / D²) i
  //
  // The state moves with the *integral* of the current, which is exactly why
  // this element remembers charge and a resistor does not.
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  const state = {
    src: 'manual' as 'manual' | 'ac' | 'pulse',
    win: 'hard' as 'hard' | 'soft',
    vs: 0, // live drive volts, or the amplitude in AC / pulse
    // 1 Hz at the default amplitude swings the boundary over roughly 0.35..0.83
    // without ever touching a rail, which is the loop at its fattest before
    // saturation starts flattening it into two plain resistor lines.
    freq: 1, // Hz
    ron: 100, // Ω
    roff: 16000, // Ω
    D: 10e-9, // m
    mu: 1e-14, // m²/(V·s)
    rate: 1,
    running: true,
  };

  const X0 = 0.35; // where the boundary sits after a reset
  let x = X0; // w/D, the one state variable
  let q = 0; // charge that has been through, C
  let phi = 0; // flux linkage, Wb
  let clock = 0; // simulated seconds since reset
  let drift = 0; // a phase used to shuffle the vacancy dots along

  /** dx per coulomb: the whole device in one number. */
  const kq = () => (state.mu * state.ron) / (state.D * state.D);
  const mem = () => state.ron * x + state.roff * (1 - x);

  /**
   * How freely the boundary moves near the edges. `hard` lets it run right up
   * to the wall and stop; `soft` is the Joglekar window, which throttles the
   * drift to nothing at both ends and can strand the state there.
   */
  function window_(xx: number) {
    if (state.win === 'hard') return 1;
    const u = 2 * xx - 1;
    return 1 - u * u * u * u; // p = 2
  }

  function vSource(tt: number) {
    if (state.src === 'manual') return state.vs;
    const s = Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * state.freq * tt);
    return state.src === 'ac' ? state.vs * s : state.vs * Math.sign(s || 1);
  }

  type Sample = { t: number; v: number; i: number; x: number };
  let hist: Sample[] = [];
  let loop: { v: number; i: number; t: number }[] = [];
  let pq: { q: number; phi: number }[] = [];

  function reset() {
    x = X0;
    q = 0;
    phi = 0;
    clock = 0;
    drift = 0;
    hist = [];
    loop = [];
    pq = [];
  }

  function physics(dtReal: number) {
    const dt = dtReal * state.rate;
    const steps = 48;
    const h = dt / steps;
    for (let s = 0; s < steps; s++) {
      clock += h;
      const v = vSource(clock);
      const i = v / mem();
      q += i * h;
      phi += v * h;
      x = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, x + kq() * i * window_(x) * h));
      drift += i * h * 4e4;
      // sampled well inside the frame, so a fast loop still draws smoothly
      if (s % 6 === 0) {
        loop.push({ v, i, t: clock });
        pq.push({ q, phi });
      }
    }
    const v = vSource(clock);
    hist.push({ t: clock, v, i: v / mem(), x });

    const span = histSpan();
    while (hist.length > 2 && hist[0].t < clock - span) hist.shift();
    const lspan = state.src === 'manual' ? 4 : 2 / state.freq;
    while (loop.length > 2 && loop[0].t < clock - lspan) loop.shift();
    if (loop.length > 1400) loop.splice(0, loop.length - 1400);
    if (pq.length > 2600) pq.splice(0, pq.length - 2600);
  }

  const histSpan = () => (state.src === 'manual' ? 6 : Math.max(2, 4 / state.freq));

  // --- formatting ------------------------------------------------------------

  function eng(v: number, unit: string, digits = 2): string {
    const a = Math.abs(v);
    if (a === 0) return `0 ${unit}`;
    const steps: [number, string][] = [
      [1e-15, 'f'], [1e-12, 'p'], [1e-9, 'n'], [1e-6, 'µ'], [1e-3, 'm'],
      [1, ''], [1e3, 'k'], [1e6, 'M'], [1e9, 'G'],
    ];
    let pick = steps[0];
    for (const s of steps) if (a >= s[0]) pick = s;
    return `${(v / pick[0]).toFixed(digits)} ${pick[1]}${unit}`;
  }
  const fmtR = (r: number) =>
    r >= 1e6 ? (r / 1e6).toFixed(r >= 1e7 ? 0 : 1) + ' MΩ'
    : r >= 1000 ? (r / 1000).toFixed(r >= 1e4 ? 0 : 1) + ' kΩ'
    : r.toFixed(0) + ' Ω';

  // --- canvas ----------------------------------------------------------------

  const canvas = document.getElementById('mr') as HTMLCanvasElement;
  const { ctx, W, H } = setupCanvas(canvas, () => draw());
  const cssVar = (n: string) => getComputedStyle(canvas).getPropertyValue(n).trim();
  const inkRGB = () => cssVar('--stage-ink') || '232,233,236';
  const inkA = (a: number) => `rgba(${inkRGB()},${a})`;
  const bg = () => cssVar('--stage-bg') || '#0d0e12';
  const { label, textWidth } = makeText(ctx, inkA);

  const ACC = '#7c8cff';
  const WARM = '#f59e0b'; // voltage
  const GREEN = '#34d399'; // current
  const VAC = '#5eead4'; // an oxygen vacancy
  const HOT = '#f9736a';

  const FOUR = { x: 20, y: 70, w: 960, h: 48 };
  const SCENE = { x: 20, y: 148, w: 960, h: 396 };
  const SCOPE = { x: 20, y: 600, w: 400, h: 250 };
  const LOOP = { x: 444, y: 600, w: 290, h: 250 };
  const PHIQ = { x: 758, y: 600, w: 222, h: 250 };

  function rr(x0: number, y0: number, w: number, h: number, r: number) {
    const rad = Math.min(r, Math.abs(w) / 2, Math.abs(h) / 2);
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(x0 + rad, y0);
    ctx.lineTo(x0 + w - rad, y0);
    ctx.quadraticCurveTo(x0 + w, y0, x0 + w, y0 + rad);
    ctx.lineTo(x0 + w, y0 + h - rad);
    ctx.quadraticCurveTo(x0 + w, y0 + h, x0 + w - rad, y0 + h);
    ctx.lineTo(x0 + rad, y0 + h);
    ctx.quadraticCurveTo(x0, y0 + h, x0, y0 + h - rad);
    ctx.lineTo(x0, y0 + rad);
    ctx.quadraticCurveTo(x0, y0, x0 + rad, y0);
    ctx.closePath();
  }
  function panel(p: { x: number; y: number; w: number; h: number }, title: string) {
    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.1);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    rr(p.x, p.y, p.w, p.h, 10);
    ctx.stroke();
    label(title, p.x + 2, p.y - 9, 0.5, 'left', 11);
  }
  function arrow(x1: number, y1: number, x2: number, y2: number, size = 5) {
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(x1, y1);
    ctx.lineTo(x2, y2);
    ctx.stroke();
    const a = Math.atan2(y2 - y1, x2 - x1);
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(x2, y2);
    ctx.lineTo(x2 - size * Math.cos(a - 0.4), y2 - size * Math.sin(a - 0.4));
    ctx.lineTo(x2 - size * Math.cos(a + 0.4), y2 - size * Math.sin(a + 0.4));
    ctx.closePath();
    ctx.fill();
  }

  // --- the missing element ---------------------------------------------------

  /**
   * Four circuit variables give six pairwise relations. Five of them were
   * spoken for; this is the sixth, and it is the only reason to call the thing
   * fundamental rather than just another two-terminal gadget.
   */
  function drawFour() {
    const items: [string, string, boolean][] = [
      ['Resistor', 'dV = R · dI', false],
      ['Capacitor', 'dQ = C · dV', false],
      ['Inductor', 'dΦ = L · dI', false],
      ['Memristor', 'dΦ = M · dQ', true],
    ];
    const bw = (FOUR.w - 3 * 16) / 4;
    items.forEach(([name, rel, on], k) => {
      const bx = FOUR.x + k * (bw + 16);
      rr(bx, FOUR.y, bw, FOUR.h, 8);
      ctx.fillStyle = on ? 'rgba(94,234,212,0.10)' : inkA(0.035);
      ctx.fill();
      if (on) {
        ctx.strokeStyle = VAC;
        ctx.lineWidth = 1.2;
        ctx.stroke();
      }
      label(name, bx + 14, FOUR.y + 19, on ? 0.9 : 0.4, 'left', 11, on ? VAC : undefined);
      label(rel, bx + 14, FOUR.y + 37, on ? 1 : 0.55, 'left', 13, on ? VAC : undefined);
    });
    label(
      'the fourth one, and the only one that needs a memory',
      FOUR.x + FOUR.w,
      FOUR.y - 9,
      0.4,
      'right',
      10
    );
  }

  // --- the film --------------------------------------------------------------

  const FILM = { x: 350, w: 480, h: 150 };
  const midY = () => SCENE.y + 165;
  const filmY = () => midY() - FILM.h / 2;

  /** Vacancy sites: a fixed scatter, so a dot appearing is the boundary moving. */
  const SITES = (() => {
    let s = 20240917;
    const rnd = () => ((s = (s * 1664525 + 1013904223) >>> 0) / 4294967296);
    const out: { u: number; v: number }[] = [];
    const COLS = 24, ROWS = 7;
    for (let c = 0; c < COLS; c++)
      for (let r = 0; r < ROWS; r++)
        out.push({
          u: (c + 0.5 + (rnd() - 0.5) * 0.7) / COLS,
          v: (r + 0.5 + (rnd() - 0.5) * 0.7) / ROWS,
        });
    return out;
  })();

  function drawFilm() {
    const y0 = filmY(), y1 = y0 + FILM.h;
    const bx = FILM.x + x * FILM.w; // the boundary
    const i = vSource(clock) / mem();

    // the two layers
    ctx.fillStyle = 'rgba(94,234,212,0.12)';
    ctx.fillRect(FILM.x, y0, x * FILM.w, FILM.h);
    ctx.fillStyle = 'rgba(245,158,11,0.07)';
    ctx.fillRect(bx, y0, (1 - x) * FILM.w, FILM.h);
    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.22);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    ctx.strokeRect(FILM.x, y0, FILM.w, FILM.h);

    // the vacancies themselves
    const moving = Math.abs(i) > 1e-7;
    const dir = Math.sign(i) || 1;
    let n = 0;
    for (const s of SITES) {
      const sx = FILM.x + s.u * FILM.w;
      const sy = y0 + s.v * FILM.h;
      if (s.u < x) {
        n++;
        // a short tail on the ones nearest the front, showing which way they drift
        if (moving && Math.abs(s.u - x) < 0.22) {
          ctx.strokeStyle = `rgba(94,234,212,${0.5 * (1 - Math.abs(s.u - x) / 0.22)})`;
          ctx.lineWidth = 1.6;
          ctx.beginPath();
          ctx.moveTo(sx - dir * 9, sy);
          ctx.lineTo(sx, sy);
          ctx.stroke();
        }
        ctx.fillStyle = VAC;
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.arc(sx, sy, 3.6, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx.fill();
      } else {
        ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.13);
        ctx.lineWidth = 1;
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.arc(sx, sy, 3, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx.stroke();
      }
    }

    // the boundary: the entire memory of the device
    ctx.strokeStyle = ACC;
    ctx.lineWidth = 3;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(bx, y0 - 8);
    ctx.lineTo(bx, y1 + 8);
    ctx.stroke();
    if (moving) {
      ctx.strokeStyle = ACC;
      ctx.fillStyle = ACC;
      ctx.lineWidth = 2;
      arrow(bx + dir * 8, y0 - 20, bx + dir * 34, y0 - 20, 7);
    }

    // the electrodes
    ctx.fillStyle = inkA(0.3);
    rr(FILM.x - 54, y0 - 10, 54, FILM.h + 20, 4);
    ctx.fill();
    rr(FILM.x + FILM.w, y0 - 10, 54, FILM.h + 20, 4);
    ctx.fill();
    label('Pt', FILM.x - 27, midY() + 4, 0.55, 'center', 11);
    label('Pt', FILM.x + FILM.w + 27, midY() + 4, 0.55, 'center', 11);

    // what the two halves are
    label(`${n} vacancies`, FILM.x + 10, y1 + 22, 0.85, 'left', 12, VAC);
    label('doped, conducting', FILM.x + 10, y1 + 40, 0.45, 'left', 10.5);
    label('undoped, insulating', FILM.x + FILM.w - 10, y1 + 22, 0.55, 'right', 12, WARM);
    label('no vacancies to carry charge', FILM.x + FILM.w - 10, y1 + 40, 0.4, 'right', 10.5);

    // the dimensions the model is written in
    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.35);
    ctx.fillStyle = inkA(0.35);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    const wy = y0 - 44;
    arrow(FILM.x, wy, bx, wy, 5);
    arrow(bx, wy, FILM.x, wy, 5);
    label(`w = ${(x * state.D * 1e9).toFixed(2)} nm`, (FILM.x + bx) / 2, wy - 8, 0.6, 'center', 11, ACC);
    const dy = y1 + 62;
    arrow(FILM.x, dy, FILM.x + FILM.w, dy, 5);
    arrow(FILM.x + FILM.w, dy, FILM.x, dy, 5);
    label(`D = ${(state.D * 1e9).toFixed(0)} nm`, FILM.x + FILM.w / 2, dy + 18, 0.5, 'center', 11);

    return { n, i };
  }

  function drawSource(sx: number, sy: number) {
    const v = vSource(clock);
    ctx.lineWidth = 2;
    if (state.src === 'manual') {
      ctx.fillStyle = bg();
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(sx, sy, 30, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.fill();
      ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.5);
      ctx.stroke();
      const ang = -Math.PI / 2 + (v / 1.5) * 2.2;
      ctx.strokeStyle = WARM;
      ctx.lineWidth = 3;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(sx, sy);
      ctx.lineTo(sx + Math.cos(ang) * 22, sy + Math.sin(ang) * 22);
      ctx.stroke();
      ctx.fillStyle = WARM;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(sx, sy, 3.6, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.fill();
    } else {
      ctx.fillStyle = bg();
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(sx, sy, 28, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.fill();
      ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.6);
      ctx.stroke();
      ctx.beginPath();
      for (let k = 0; k <= 28; k++) {
        const f = k / 28;
        const px = sx - 16 + f * 32;
        const s = Math.sin(f * Math.PI * 2);
        const py = sy - (state.src === 'ac' ? s : Math.sign(s || 1)) * 10;
        k ? ctx.lineTo(px, py) : ctx.moveTo(px, py);
      }
      ctx.stroke();
    }
    label(`${v >= 0 ? '+' : ''}${v.toFixed(3)} V`, sx, sy - 44, 0.9, 'center', 14, WARM);
    label(
      state.src === 'manual' ? 'you, driving it' : state.src === 'ac' ? 'AC source' : 'pulse train',
      sx,
      sy + 50,
      0.45,
      'center',
      11
    );
  }

  function drawScene() {
    panel(SCENE, 'INSIDE THE FILM');
    const my = midY();
    const sx = SCENE.x + 130;
    const retY = my + 172;

    // the loop the current goes round
    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.4);
    ctx.lineWidth = 2;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(sx + 30, my);
    ctx.lineTo(FILM.x - 54, my);
    ctx.moveTo(FILM.x + FILM.w + 54, my);
    ctx.lineTo(SCENE.x + SCENE.w - 30, my);
    ctx.lineTo(SCENE.x + SCENE.w - 30, retY);
    ctx.lineTo(sx, retY);
    ctx.lineTo(sx, my + 30);
    ctx.stroke();

    drawSource(sx, my);
    const { i } = drawFilm();

    // the current, drawn where it flows
    const moving = Math.abs(i) > 1e-7;
    if (moving) {
      const dir = Math.sign(i);
      ctx.strokeStyle = GREEN;
      ctx.fillStyle = GREEN;
      ctx.lineWidth = 2;
      const mx = (sx + FILM.x - 54) / 2;
      arrow(mx - dir * 30, my - 20, mx + dir * 30, my - 20, 8);
      label(eng(Math.abs(i), 'A'), mx, my - 30, 0.85, 'center', 12, GREEN);
    } else {
      label('no current', (sx + FILM.x - 54) / 2, my - 24, 0.45, 'center', 11);
      label('so the boundary is frozen', (sx + FILM.x - 54) / 2, my - 8, 0.35, 'center', 10);
    }

    // the resistance, as a bar between the two rails it lives between
    const bx = SCENE.x + 40, bw = 250, by = SCENE.y + SCENE.h - 46;
    const f = (mem() - state.ron) / Math.max(1, state.roff - state.ron);
    ctx.fillStyle = inkA(0.07);
    rr(bx, by, bw, 14, 4);
    ctx.fill();
    ctx.fillStyle = ACC;
    rr(bx, by, Math.max(3, (1 - f) * bw), 14, 4);
    ctx.fill();
    label('R_on', bx, by - 6, 0.4, 'left', 10);
    label('R_off', bx + bw, by - 6, 0.4, 'right', 10);
    label(`M = ${fmtR(mem())}`, bx + bw + 16, by + 12, 0.95, 'left', 14, ACC);
  }

  // --- scope -----------------------------------------------------------------

  function drawScope() {
    panel(SCOPE, 'VOLTAGE, CURRENT AND THE BOUNDARY');
    const px = SCOPE.x + 46, py = SCOPE.y + 18, pw = SCOPE.w - 62, ph = SCOPE.h - 52;
    const span = histSpan();
    const t1 = Math.max(span, clock), t0 = t1 - span;
    const X = (t: number) => px + ((t - t0) / span) * pw;

    let vmax = 1e-6, imax = 1e-12;
    for (const h of hist) {
      vmax = Math.max(vmax, Math.abs(h.v));
      imax = Math.max(imax, Math.abs(h.i));
    }
    const Yv = (v: number) => py + ph * 0.22 - (v / vmax) * (ph * 0.18);
    const Yi = (i: number) => py + ph * 0.62 - (i / imax) * (ph * 0.18);
    const Yx = (xx: number) => py + ph - 6 - xx * (ph * 0.26);

    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.18);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(px, py);
    ctx.lineTo(px, py + ph);
    ctx.lineTo(px + pw, py + ph);
    ctx.stroke();
    for (const [y, txt] of [
      [Yv(0), '0 V'],
      [Yi(0), '0 A'],
    ] as [number, string][]) {
      ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.12);
      ctx.setLineDash([3, 3]);
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(px, y);
      ctx.lineTo(px + pw, y);
      ctx.stroke();
      ctx.setLineDash([]);
      label(txt, px - 6, y + 4, 0.35, 'right', 10);
    }
    label('1', px - 6, Yx(1) + 4, 0.3, 'right', 9);
    label('0', px - 6, Yx(0) + 4, 0.3, 'right', 9);

    if (hist.length > 1) {
      const series: [string, (h: Sample) => number, number][] = [
        [WARM, (h) => Yv(h.v), 1.8],
        [GREEN, (h) => Yi(h.i), 1.8],
        [ACC, (h) => Yx(h.x), 2.2],
      ];
      for (const [col, fn, lw] of series) {
        ctx.strokeStyle = col;
        ctx.lineWidth = lw;
        ctx.beginPath();
        hist.forEach((h, k) => (k ? ctx.lineTo(X(h.t), fn(h)) : ctx.moveTo(X(h.t), fn(h))));
        ctx.stroke();
      }
    }
    label('voltage', px + 6, py + 12, 0.8, 'left', 10.5, WARM);
    label('current', px + 68, py + 12, 0.8, 'left', 10.5, GREEN);
    label('w/D', px + 130, py + 12, 0.8, 'left', 10.5, ACC);
    label(
      'the boundary only moves while a current flows',
      px + pw,
      py + ph + 18,
      0.4,
      'right',
      10
    );
  }

  // --- the pinched loop ------------------------------------------------------

  function drawLoop() {
    panel(LOOP, 'CURRENT AGAINST VOLTAGE');
    const px = LOOP.x + 40, py = LOOP.y + 20, pw = LOOP.w - 58, ph = LOOP.h - 62;
    const cx = px + pw / 2, cy = py + ph / 2;
    let vmax = 1e-6, imax = 1e-12;
    for (const s of loop) {
      vmax = Math.max(vmax, Math.abs(s.v));
      imax = Math.max(imax, Math.abs(s.i));
    }
    const X = (v: number) => cx + (v / vmax) * (pw / 2) * 0.9;
    const Y = (i: number) => cy - (i / imax) * (ph / 2) * 0.9;

    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.16);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(px, cy);
    ctx.lineTo(px + pw, cy);
    ctx.moveTo(cx, py);
    ctx.lineTo(cx, py + ph);
    ctx.stroke();
    label('V', px + pw, cy + 14, 0.35, 'right', 10);
    label('I', cx + 8, py + 8, 0.35, 'left', 10);

    // the trace, fading into the past so the direction of travel reads
    if (loop.length > 2) {
      for (let k = 1; k < loop.length; k++) {
        const f = k / loop.length;
        ctx.strokeStyle = `rgba(52,211,153,${(0.08 + 0.75 * f * f).toFixed(3)})`;
        ctx.lineWidth = 1.1 + 1.4 * f;
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.moveTo(X(loop[k - 1].v), Y(loop[k - 1].i));
        ctx.lineTo(X(loop[k].v), Y(loop[k].i));
        ctx.stroke();
      }
      const last = loop[loop.length - 1];
      ctx.fillStyle = GREEN;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(X(last.v), Y(last.i), 4, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.fill();
    }

    // the pinch: the one point every memristor loop has to pass through
    ctx.strokeStyle = HOT;
    ctx.lineWidth = 1.6;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.arc(cx, cy, 7, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx.stroke();
    label('pinched here', cx + 11, cy - 9, 0.75, 'left', 10, HOT);
    label('v = M i, so i = 0 forces v = 0', px, py + ph + 18, 0.45, 'left', 10);
    label(
      state.src === 'manual'
        ? 'switch to AC to close the loop'
        : `${state.freq.toFixed(2)} Hz · faster driving flattens it into a line`,
      px,
      py + ph + 34,
      0.4,
      'left',
      10
    );
  }

  // --- the constitutive curve ------------------------------------------------

  function drawPhiQ() {
    panel(PHIQ, 'FLUX AGAINST CHARGE');
    const px = PHIQ.x + 40, py = PHIQ.y + 20, pw = PHIQ.w - 56, ph = PHIQ.h - 62;

    let q0 = 0, q1 = 0, p0 = 0, p1 = 0;
    for (const s of pq) {
      q0 = Math.min(q0, s.q); q1 = Math.max(q1, s.q);
      p0 = Math.min(p0, s.phi); p1 = Math.max(p1, s.phi);
    }
    const qs = Math.max(1e-9, (q1 - q0) * 0.6 + 1e-12);
    const ps = Math.max(1e-9, (p1 - p0) * 0.6 + 1e-12);
    const qm = (q0 + q1) / 2, pm = (p0 + p1) / 2;
    const X = (qq: number) => px + pw / 2 + ((qq - qm) / qs) * (pw / 2) * 0.85;
    const Y = (pp: number) => py + ph / 2 - ((pp - pm) / ps) * (ph / 2) * 0.85;

    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.16);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(px, Y(pm));
    ctx.lineTo(px + pw, Y(pm));
    ctx.moveTo(X(qm), py);
    ctx.lineTo(X(qm), py + ph);
    ctx.stroke();
    label('q', px + pw, Y(pm) + 14, 0.35, 'right', 10);
    label('Φ', X(qm) + 8, py + 8, 0.35, 'left', 10);

    // The device's own curve, φ(q) = ∫M dq, drawn over the range in which the
    // boundary is still free to move. The trace has to lie on it whatever the
    // drive is doing, which is what makes M a property of the device and not of
    // the experiment. A sticky boundary makes the state path-dependent, so the
    // curve is only claimed for the hard-stop case.
    if (state.win === 'hard') {
      const k = kq();
      const qlo = -X0 / k, qhi = (1 - X0) / k;
      const dR = state.roff - state.ron;
      const phiOf = (qq: number) => state.roff * qq - dR * (X0 * qq + (k * qq * qq) / 2);
      ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.3);
      ctx.setLineDash([4, 4]);
      ctx.lineWidth = 1.4;
      ctx.beginPath();
      for (let n = 0; n <= 60; n++) {
        const qq = qlo + ((qhi - qlo) * n) / 60;
        const px2 = X(qq), py2 = Y(phiOf(qq));
        n ? ctx.lineTo(px2, py2) : ctx.moveTo(px2, py2);
      }
      ctx.stroke();
      ctx.setLineDash([]);
    }

    if (pq.length > 2) {
      ctx.strokeStyle = VAC;
      ctx.lineWidth = 2.2;
      ctx.beginPath();
      pq.forEach((s, k) => (k ? ctx.lineTo(X(s.q), Y(s.phi)) : ctx.moveTo(X(s.q), Y(s.phi))));
      ctx.stroke();
      const last = pq[pq.length - 1];
      ctx.fillStyle = VAC;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(X(last.q), Y(last.phi), 4, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.fill();
    }
    label(
      state.win === 'hard' ? 'the slope of this curve is M' : 'a sticky boundary loses the curve',
      px - 24,
      py + ph + 18,
      0.45,
      'left',
      10
    );
    label('drive it any way you like', px - 24, py + ph + 34, 0.4, 'left', 10);
  }

  // --- readouts --------------------------------------------------------------

  const el = (id: string) => document.getElementById(id) as HTMLElement;
  const setRow = (n: number, lab: string, val: string) => {
    el('l' + n).innerHTML = subHtml(lab);
    el('r' + n).textContent = val;
  };
  function updateReadout() {
    const v = vSource(clock);
    const i = v / mem();
    setRow(1, 'Voltage V', v.toFixed(3) + ' V');
    setRow(2, 'Current I', eng(i, 'A'));
    setRow(3, 'Resistance M', fmtR(mem()));
    setRow(4, 'State w/D', x.toFixed(4));
    setRow(5, 'Charge through q', eng(q, 'C'));
    setRow(6, 'Flux linkage Φ', eng(phi, 'Wb'));
    setRow(7, 'On/off ratio', (state.roff / state.ron).toFixed(0) + '×');
  }

  // --- loop ------------------------------------------------------------------

  function draw() {
    ctx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);
    label('Memristor', 20, 30, 0.85, 'left', 14);
    label(
      state.src === 'manual'
        ? 'push charge through and the boundary keeps a record of it'
        : state.src === 'ac'
          ? 'drive it back and forth and the loop closes, pinched at the origin'
          : 'pulses latch it between a low and a high resistance',
      20,
      52,
      0.5,
      'left',
      11,
      VAC
    );
    const legend: [string, string][] = [
      [VAC, 'oxygen vacancy'],
      [ACC, 'boundary'],
      [GREEN, 'current'],
    ];
    let lx = W - 20;
    for (let k = legend.length - 1; k >= 0; k--) {
      const [c, tx] = legend[k];
      const tw = textWidth(tx, 11);
      label(tx, lx, 30, 0.55, 'right', 11);
      ctx.fillStyle = c;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(lx - tw - 11, 26, 5, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.fill();
      lx -= tw + 32;
    }
    drawFour();
    drawScene();
    drawScope();
    drawLoop();
    drawPhiQ();
  }

  let last = performance.now();
  function frame(now: number) {
    let dt = (now - last) / 1000;
    last = now;
    dt = Math.min(0.05, Math.max(0, dt));
    if (state.running) physics(dt);
    draw();
    updateReadout();
    requestAnimationFrame(frame);
  }

  // --- controls --------------------------------------------------------------

  const runBtn = el('run');
  runBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
    state.running = !state.running;
    runBtn.textContent = state.running ? 'Pause' : 'Run';
  });
  el('reset').addEventListener('click', reset);

  let ready = false;
  function bindRange(id: string, apply: (n: number) => void, restart = false) {
    const inp = el(id) as HTMLInputElement;
    const run = () => {
      apply(+inp.value);
      if (restart && ready) reset();
    };
    inp.addEventListener('input', run);
    run();
  }
  bindRange('vs', (n) => {
    state.vs = n / 100;
    el('vsval').textContent = `${state.vs.toFixed(2)} V`;
  });
  bindRange('freq', (n) => {
    state.freq = n / 100;
    el('fval').textContent = `${state.freq.toFixed(2)} Hz`;
  });
  bindRange('ron', (n) => {
    state.ron = n;
    el('ronval').textContent = fmtR(state.ron);
  });
  bindRange('roff', (n) => {
    state.roff = n * 100;
    el('roffval').textContent = fmtR(state.roff);
  });
  bindRange('d', (n) => {
    state.D = n * 1e-9;
    el('dval').textContent = `${n} nm`;
  }, true);
  bindRange('mu', (n) => {
    state.mu = (n / 100) * 1e-14;
    el('muval').textContent = eng(state.mu, 'm²/Vs', 1);
  });
  bindRange('rate', (n) => {
    state.rate = n / 100;
    el('rateval').textContent = `${state.rate.toFixed(1)}×`;
  });

  function syncControls() {
    el('ctl-f').style.display = state.src === 'manual' ? 'none' : '';
    el('vlab').textContent = state.src === 'manual' ? 'Drive it yourself' : 'Amplitude';
    el('vhint').textContent = state.src === 'manual' ? 'drag me up and down' : 'peak volts';
    const inp = el('vs') as HTMLInputElement;
    inp.min = state.src === 'manual' ? '-150' : '0';
    if (state.src !== 'manual' && +inp.value <= 0) inp.value = '100';
    state.vs = +inp.value / 100;
    el('vsval').textContent = `${state.vs.toFixed(2)} V`;
  }

  el('src').addEventListener('click', (e) => {
    const btn = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('button');
    if (!btn) return;
    document.querySelectorAll('#src button').forEach((b) => b.classList.remove('active'));
    btn.classList.add('active');
    state.src = btn.dataset.s as 'manual' | 'ac' | 'pulse';
    syncControls();
    reset();
  });
  el('win').addEventListener('click', (e) => {
    const btn = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('button');
    if (!btn) return;
    document.querySelectorAll('#win button').forEach((b) => b.classList.remove('active'));
    btn.classList.add('active');
    state.win = btn.dataset.w as 'hard' | 'soft';
  });

  syncControls();
  reset();
  ready = true;
  requestAnimationFrame(frame);
</script>

<style>
  .mr-canvas {
    touch-action: none;
  }
  .scale-hint {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    margin-top: 3px;
  }
</style>
